  "name": "Question 4",
  "problem": "Ann chooses a card at random from a deck of cards labeled $28$ through $65.$  What is the expected value of the chosen number?",
  "worked_solution": "Let $X$ represent the value of the number chosen. From the problem statement, we know that $X∼U\\{28,29,…,65\\},$ and we wish to compute $\\text{E}[X].$\n\nIn general, if $X∼U\\{a,a+1,…,b\\},$ then $X$ has the following expected value:\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[X]=\\frac{a+b}{2}\n$$\n\nSo, for our random variable $X∼U\\{28,29,…,65\\},$ we have the following expected value:\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[X]=\\frac{28+65}{2}=46.5\n$$\n\nTherefore, the expected value of the chosen number is $46.5.$",
